---
Changes since v3:
- execute_function_todo no longer tests targetm.asm_out.jump_table_base,
  which only AArch64 defines.  For the opt-out model, verify_jump_tables
  now checks all jump tables on all targets, also on ports that opt out.
- While the CFG exists, verify_jump_tables now checks the new rule of
  patch 2/8: a shared table in use follows a jump through it.  After
  free_cfg, machine reorganization can put insns between them.
- gcc.dg/plugin/tablejump-misplaced-table.c is a new negative test.  Its
  plugin case misplaced_table moves the table and label after a block
  that does not jump through the table (new helper non_user_block).
- Commit message: it says "all targets" and describes the new check.  It
  drops the bootstrap line, because the cover letter gives the
  validation.
- rtlanal.cc now includes tree-pass.h for PROP_cfg.  The ChangeLog names
  this include and hash-map.h, which v3 included but did not name.

